%N A402442 a(n) = A402441(A102476(n)); smallest k in [1,N] coprime to N such that -k is a quadratic residue modulo N, N = A102476(n).
%C A402442 N = A102476(n) is the least number such that the multiplicative group of integers modulo N has 2^n square roots of 1.
%C A402442 a(n) is the minimal element of the coset of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing -1, where N = A102476(n), (Z/NZ)* is the multiplicative group of integers modulo N and (Z/NZ)*^2 is the subgroup of squares.
%F A402442 a(n) = A102476(n) - A402441(n) for n > 0.
%e A402442 List of negated squares modulo N = 1, 3, 8, 24, 120, 840, 9240 in A102476:
%e A402442   1
%e A402442   2
%e A402442   7
%e A402442   23
%e A402442   71, 119
%e A402442   311, 479, 551, 671, 719, 839
%e A402442   479, 1151, 1319, 1559, 1679, 2351, 2999, 3071, 3671, 3911, 4199, 4751, 4919, 5519, 5711, 5759, 6431, 6551, 6599, 7031, 7391, 7559, 7871, 8279, 8399, 8711, 8879, 8951, 9071, 9239
%o A402442 (PARI) a(n) = if(n<=1, [1, 2][n+1], A402441( 4*factorback(primes(n-1)) )) \\ see A402441 for its program
